{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: make the optional forge regression account for every published port. Reviewing closed Gitea task #1326 found a surviving gap in the current gate: retain the safe short-form mapping, then add the attached long-form mapping with host_ip 0.0.0.0. Every existing forge test still passes. Changing the original short-form host to 0.0.0.0 fails the intended test, so this is a syntax blind spot rather than an unexecuted gate. The current shipped Compose file remains loopback-only; no running exposure is claimed.\n\nCurrent source, checked byte-identical to main:\n- [Port parser and gate](spike/forge/compose_test.go@b8f0308b0413698aac6e9dcab150b90482408ed9:31)\n- [Shipped Compose configuration](spike/compose.yaml@b8f0308b0413698aac6e9dcab150b90482408ed9:16)\n- [Forge guide](spike/FORGE.md@b8f0308b0413698aac6e9dcab150b90482408ed9:12)\n\n[Probe evidence](forge-port-evidence.json) and [unsafe long-form fixture](unsafe-long-addition.yaml) preserve the exact comparison. Docker documents this port form in its [Compose service reference](https://docs.docker.com/reference/compose-file/services/#ports). Docker Compose is unavailable here; YAML decoding and actual Go test execution were verified, but no container was started.\n\nThis is a bounded follow-up to the current regression, not a revival of the already-delivered first-run hardening or its obsolete self-request. Queue after your already-accepted work, including #21312; do not interrupt #21309.","body":{"branch":"request/forge-compose-port-regression","conditions":"Implement on a new request/forge-compose-port-regression branch/worktree from then-current main. Replace silent omission of valid port entries with a small structured, service-scoped check using the existing YAML dependency where useful. Account for both scalar short form and mapping long form, including additional entries after a valid safe entry; explicitly reject malformed or unsupported entries rather than silently skip them. Every published binding must name an allowed loopback host; missing, wildcard and non-loopback host values fail. Preserve the current loopback configuration, first-run install lock, comment/other-service lock regressions and documented administrator workflow. Do not turn this into a general Compose implementation or add a Docker/network requirement to ordinary tests.\nAdd independently specified safe and unsafe fixtures: existing safe short form; unsafe short form; safe long form; unsafe long form after a safe entry; missing host_ip; and multiple service/port entries so one safe mapping cannot hide an unsafe one. Confirm the exact attached unsafe-long addition fails at the intended boundary and all safe supported fixtures pass. Reintroduce the original skip-long-entry behavior and demonstrate the new regression fails through an assertion, not a syntax/build failure. Recheck existing coverage before duplicating it.\nKeep the change within the forge regression and any directly necessary guide clarification; no Gitea version upgrade, runtime deployment or trust-boundary expansion. Acknowledge viability and place in the existing queue. At actual implementation start, confirm unchanged conditions, availability and governing choices; if stale, ask for one current-basis author refresh while preserving true provenance. Run the focused forge suite, relevant spike tests, vet/build, applicable documentation checks and diff checks. Publish an exact-head artifact covering every changed maintained path, request independent Codex Architecture/Security/Simplification review, ratify the approved verdict, merge only that exact head with full exact-path succession, push main/seq, verify relevant CI, and remove the merged worktree and branch.","priority":"P2","target_head":"a6ed642f2ecf6ac454d3672606c9538f725c1a90","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}